SUMMARY:Arab Heritage Month Crafts at FLIP
DESCRIPTION:FLIP has a variety of crafts for different age levels this month to honor Arab Heritage Month. \n\nKhanda Mosaics: Use coloring pages\, glue\, and tissue paper to create beautiful\, traditional designs.\nMala Bracelets: Make your own bracelets with beads\, which may require adult help to finish\nArabic Alphabet Caligraphy: Use a traditional brush and ink to learn how to write and read Arabic letters – from right to left\, of course\nBedouin Weave Craft: Cut and paste colorful paper to mirror the kinds of patterns used in traditional weaving.\n\nOf course\, all our normal exhibits are available as well\, like our green screen stage\, cartoon-making room\, and fort making area. \n$10/Person\, Under Age 2 is Free \nEditor’s note: This event is a community submission.
URL:https://pdxparent.com/event-single/arab-heritage-month-crafts-at-flip/2026-04-24/
LOCATION:The FLIP Children’s Museum of Hillsboro\, 136 SE 3rd Ave Ste 200\, Hillsboro\, OR\, 97123\, United States
CATEGORIES:Arts/Crafts,Educational,Family Fun,Indoor Play Park,Kids Calendar
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://pdxparent.com/wp-content/uploads/ARAB-HERITAGE-MONTH.png
END:VEVENT
